"Today I am here to share with you the washi tape initial wall art that I made as part of the collage wall that I put together when I helped my dad redecorate his family room. I love the way this giant initial turned out! My dad was a bit skeptical about the bicycle washi tape, but I think a little whimsy in life is a good thing, don\u2019t you?\nLet\u2019s talk about how I created this fun washi tape wall art. I started with a GIANT wooden letter, which I believe I found at Hobby Lobby (use a coupon!). I painted the top of the letter white, so that the thinner washi would have a white background, and the edges of the letter black, so that it would match the frames on the wall. Here is what happened next . . .\nNext I just started going for it with the washi. I laid it out in strips across the letter and didn\u2019t worry about trimming until the end. I also chose not to do an exact pattern, but mixed it up a bit. I did try to space the bicycles out fairly evenly, though, since they really stand out on the letter. One of the things that I love about washi is that you can always reposition it if you don\u2019t like where you placed it initially, similar to masking tape.\nTo finish up, I trimmed the edges of the washi tape off and then I painted a thin layer of Mod Podge on top of the washi and just over the edges to seal everything firmly to the letter.\nAll done! What do you think? Now let\u2019s take a look at the wall art in action, shall we?\nI am so excited about the way that my washi tape initial wall art turned out. It is such a fun addition to our family room gallery wall. Now go get busy and make your own!\nLove it, it looks great! Thanks for sharing this at the Dishing It & Digging It Link Party.\nI have a bunch of washing tape in my stash, and I forget to do anything with it. Your big \u201cW\u201d looks great! I love the patterns in your black & white washing tape. It looks great on your gallery wall."
