"Registration is now open for the 15th annual Kent Cornucopia Days Fun Run and Walk, scheduled for Saturday, July 14, at 9 a.m.\nAccording to Kent Parks program coordinator Mark Hendrickson, the race has become a summer tradition for many residents throughout Puget Sound.\n\u201cThe course is U.S. Track and Field certified and is one of the few flat courses in the area. We\u2019ll have awards for the top five finishers in each age group. Participants age 60 and over run for free courtesy of Kent Bowl,\u201d Hendrickson said.\nHosted by the Kent Parks, Recreation and Community Servicers, the race entree fee is $10 or $25 (with a technical T-shirt) before July 13.\nRegister online at Active.com or pick up registration forms at the Kent Commons and many Puget Sound athletic stores.\nAvoid the lines on race day \u2013 pick up shirts and bibs on Wednesday, July 11 between 3 and 7 p.m. at Road Runner Sports at Kent Station.\nRace day registration and packet pick up is also available near the start/finish line at 7:30 a.m.\nFor more information, visit KentArts.com or call 253-856-5050."
