"It's more handy than it looks.\nOver the past eight years, we've seen a lot of brilliant inventions and smart business ventures on Shark Tank\u2014so it's a little hard to believe that the most successful product to come out of the ABC reality show so far is a tiny, smiling sponge. Don't let its size fool you, though.\nAaron Krause introduced Scrub Daddy to the \"sharks\" in 2012, and entrepreneur Lori Greiner offered $200,000 for a 20 percent stake in the company. Since then, the sponge has sold over 10 million units, resulting in over $50 million in sales, according to INSIDER.\nSo what exactly makes this little foam guy so special? Due to its exclusive FlexTexture material, the Scrub Daddy changes its texture depending on the water temperature. For instance, placing the sponge under warm water turns it into your average soft sponge, perfect for washing dishes or wiping countertops. But soak the sponge in cold water, and it becomes so firm that you can give any dirty pot or pan a good, hard scrub, no harsh chemical cleaning products needed.The scratch-free foam can be used to clean silverware, too, and it even self-cleans.\nIf that video didn't convince you that the Scrub Daddy is brilliant, its 4.5 star rating on Amazon might change your tune. With over 2,000 reviews, the product has received tons of praise from customers. \"I was a little skeptical of these 'self cleaning' sponges,'\" one commenter wrote. \"I use sponges regularly and they always get messy and difficult to work with. It was time to buy some new sponges so I figured I'd give these a try and see if they lived up to the hype. Sure enough, they did.\"\n\"I love, love, love these! The soft when hot, hard when cold [feature] is awesome,\" another commenter wrote. \"I won't use any other sponge ever again!\"\nThe Scrub Daddy brand has now expanded to include other cleaning products including the Big Daddy and the Scrub Mommy, with a dual-sided scrubber and sponge. Want to see what all the hype's about? You can purchase the original Scrub Daddy in a pack of four for $14.92 on Amazon."
"Offensive Tackle Drew Richmond is one of the hottest commodities on the Graduate Transfer market.\nRichmond entered his name into the Transfer portal on January 11th.\nAfter redshirting his first season at Tennessee, Richmond started in 25 of the 28 games he played in for the Volunteers the following three seasons. In his first two years on the field, Richmond played strictly at Left Tackle, but played every snap last season at Right Tackle (started all 12 games).\nComing out of High School, 247Sports ranked Richmond as the #56 overall player in the nation, and Rivals and ESPN both ranked him as the #1 player in the state of Tennessee in the 2015 class. Both 247Sports and Rivals rated him as a 5-star prospect.\nRichmond took an official visit to USC on March 23rd, Florida State on March 29th, and Oklahoma State this past weekend. NC State is hoping that they get the 4th.\nNC State\u2019s Band of Brothers were one of the best offensive line units in the nation last year, but three of the starters graduated, and will all be playing in the NFL next year.\nWhile starting Right Guard Joshua Fedd-Jackson (JR) and Right Tackle Justin Witt (RS JR) return, the possible addition of Richmond on the Left side would be a glorious addition. Redshirt Junior Joe Sculthorpe will fill the big shoes of Garrett Bradbury at Center in 2019. He served as the 6th man on the Wolfpack offensive line in 2018, and was 5th highest graded offensive lineman in the ACC last season according to ProFootballFocus."
"An arrangement of the utopic workers' tune that avoids anthemism by starting with a bass-driven hip-hop beat and breaking into a swing blues for the choruses. Quotations from Aaron Copeland (\"Fanfare for the Common Man\"), Bob Marley (\"Get Up Stand Up\"), Missy Eliott (\"Work it\") and Cypress Hill (\"Real Estate,\" ironically enough) enliven matters.\ntrade union groups that focused on the working class and class struggle. Following an international Socialist congress in Copenhagen in 1910, the song was officially adopted by those present as the Socialist anthem.\nstudents in Tiananmen Square in 1989.\nwhich they decided the lyrics were out of touch with modern activist movements. Billy Bragg recently performed his version a capella at Pete Seeger's 90th birthday concert, in celebration of the folk singer and in solidarity with workers around the world, which I think speaks to the lasting power and importance of this song."
"Toki Tori 2+: a big plus on Steam!\nBig news for all Steam gamers: Toki Tori 2+ will be released on July 11th!\nYes, you read it correctly; there is a \u2018+\u2019 behind the game\u2019s name. We decided to change the name to Toki Tori 2+, to reflect the many new additions and changes we have made for this version.\nFrom the day that we announced the game, back in 2011, the Steam community has supported us with countless feedback reports, play-through sessions and a lot of testing. Because of this and the long delays, we strongly feel that we owe the Steam community big time. It\u2019s time for us to put money where our mouth is.\nThe game won\u2019t be simply a Steam rendition of the Wii U version. Instead we\u2019ve improved the gameplay and presentation across the board. And to justify the name change, we also added a level editor, Steam Workshop integration, a lot of achievements and more puzzles!\nStill no eggs? Well, at least now we have eggplants!\nEver since the Wii U release back in April, we have been in close contact with our community. We talked to many gamers and reviewers and asked them if they could share their experiences with us. We listened and decided to address a number of issues in an initial update on the Wii U.\nHowever, for Toki Tori 2+ we are taking things a step further. Just to name a few changes: to prevent players from getting stuck early on, we added a new mechanic to guide them through the early part of the game. Furthermore we added several gates to make sure you can reach your intended destination more efficiently. We improved the world map, giving players a better understanding of where they are in the game. We also improved the presentation of the game and added several landmarks to the surroundings. Not only do they look nice; they will also help the player to better understand its position on the world map.\nA Dutch game without windmills? Impossible!\nToki Tori 2+ will ship with a level editor, allowing you make your own Toki Tori 2+ levels! Obviously having a level editor without being able to share your creations with others, wouldn\u2019t be that much fun. Therefore we added Steam Workshop integration, making it very easy for you to share your awesome creations with the rest of the world.\nPro tip of the day: don\u2019t forget how to solve your own level!\nInterested in the Beta? Apply now and help us tweak the editor and Steam Workshop integration.\nBe sure to keep an eye out on our website, as we\u2019ll be posting more information on Toki Tori 2+ soon!"
