"The Todman Stakes, also known as the Todman Slipper Trial, is a Group 2 race for two-year-old colts and geldings held on Randwick Guineas Day at Royal Randwick during the Sydney Autumn Racing Carnival.\nContested on a Saturday in early to mid March each season the set weights event is a key support act at a meeting that also hosts the Group 1 Royal Randwick Guineas (1600m) and Group 1 Canterbury Stakes (1300m).\nThe Todman Stakes offers $300,000 in prize money including $180,000 to the winner and takes place over a 1200m sprint distance. It is the male juveniles\u2019 equivalent of the Group 2 $300,000 Reisling Stakes (1200m) for the fillies and both races are traditional lead-ups to the Group 1 $3.5 million Golden Slipper Stakes (1200m) run a fortnight later.\nThe Todman Stakes winner is exempt from Golden Slipper Stakes ballot and the double was most recently achieved by Vancouver (2015) and Pierro (2012).\nThe latest edition of the Todman Stakes takes place on Saturday March 9, 2019.\nThe full Todman Stakes 2019 results & finishing order revealing the winner of the Golden Slipper ballot exemption will be published below after the race takes place on Saturday March 9, 2019.\nIt was an upset 2018 Todman Stakes Result after race favourite Performer threw off his jockey Hugh Bowman during the run leaving the Jean Dubois-trained Aylmerton from Goulburn to win at big odds after a Canterbury victory on debut the run prior.\nTodman Stakes odds favour colts and geldings with previous winning form in Sydney. Proven ability at least over 1100m is key to the Todman Stakes betting markets as is previous experience in black-type company.\nFavourites have a solid Todman Stakes record however in 2014 Ghibellines scored an upset as a 40/1 shot in betting only a few years after Smart Missile won at 20/1 in 2011.\nThe updated Todman Stakes 2019 betting odds will be made available below once released for you to back the key Golden Slipper Stakes contenders at the best autumn markets.\nThe Todman Stakes or Todman Slipper Trial field attracts a line-up of the season\u2019s most promising young two-year-old colts and geldings on the Golden Slipper Stakes path.\nVancouver (2015) recently completed the Todman Stakes \u2013 Golden Slipper Stakes double. Photo Credit: Steve Hart.\nThe race usually features youngsters coming out of races like the Group 3 Canonbury Stakes (1100m) in January, February\u2019s Listed Lonhro Plate (1100m) or the Group 2 Silver Slipper Stakes (1100m) a fortnight earlier.\nThe last horse to complete the Silver Slipper Stakes \u2013 Todman Stakes double was Pierro (2012) who also won the Golden Slipper, ATC Sires\u2019 Produce Stakes and Champagne Stakes in Group 1 company at his next three starts.\nTodman Stakes nominations close on the Monday before the race followed by the final field of acceptances and barrier draw on the Wednesday.\nThe official Todman Stakes 2019 Field of Golden Slipper-bound two-year-olds will be published below on the Wednesday before Royal Randwick Guineas Day.\nThe early Todman Stakes 2019 nominations are open until the Monday of race week and will be available here once announced.\nTodman Stakes tips include looking for non-maidens with previous winning form in Sydney over 1100m or 1200m that hail from the state\u2019s leading stables including Gai Waterhouse who prepared Vancouver (2015) and Pierro (2012) to victory in recent years.\nOur insider Todman Stakes betting tips for 2019 will be available below leading-up to the Group 2 sprint so stay tuned for the two-year-old gallopers to back and sack this season.\nThe Todman Stakes form guide lists all of the essential information needed before placing a bet including barriers, jockeys, trainers and barriers.\nGai Waterhouse has a good training record in the race as well as the Golden Slipper Stakes so looking for in-form youngsters prepared by her on the Todman Slipper Trial form guide is a good tip.\nThe Todman Stakes form has held-up in the Golden Slipper a number of times in recent years with Vancouver (2015) doing the double before Capitalist improved on a lead-up second in the Todman to take out the world\u2019s richest race for juveniles.\nA link to our comprehensive Todman Stakes 2019 Form Guide will be provided for punters below the week of the race.\nThere has been a number of upset Todman Stakes results in recent years, but the set weights conditions of the race usually favours the classier two-year-old males in the field.\nNotable recent Todman Stakes winners include Vancouver (2015), Criterion (2013), Pierro (2012), Written Tycoon (2005), Charge Forward (2004) and Exceed And Excel (2003)."
