"This section of Conejo Valley Guide highlights local professional groups and service organizations in Ventura County and surrounding areas, including Thousand Oaks, Westlake Village, Newbury Park, Agoura Hills, Calabasas, Malibu, Camarillo, Oxnard, Port Hueneme, Ventura, Somis, Moorpark, Simi Valley, Ojai, Santa Paula and Fillmore.\nFounded October 30, 1916, 5 years before the State of California was chartered!\nWomen's advocacy, education and research group; chartered in 1966!\nPhilanthropic organization founded in 1995. 100% of donations go towards programs.\nGroup for professionals professionals involved in corporate growth, development and mergers and acquisitions initiatives in the West Valley-Ventura County-Santa Barbara areas.\nNon-profit volunteer service club for many local events and emergency preparedness.\nService Unit Site for Girl Scouts of Newbury Park; meets 1st Thursday of the month.\nChartered in November 1966; meets at lunch on Tuesdays.\nFounded in 1965; meets on Wednesday mornings.\nMeets on Wednesday mornings in T.O.\nFounded in 1925; meets Fridays at noon.\nWomens' service/fundraising organization in Camarillo that has raised funds for local non-profits since 1972.\nMeets Thursdays at 7 am.\nA compilation of links to local programs!\nThere are about 40 different clubs in Ventura County!\nVolunteer organization established by Congress to assist the Coast Guard in promoting boating safety."
