"Exclusive: DFI's fabled LANParty motherboard range is no more. Here's the story behind why.\nIt's teeny, it's tiny, it's DFI's MI P55-T36 mini-ITX motherboard! Performance P55 meets small form factor, and we compare the MI P55-T36 to its full size ATX brothers to see if keeps up with the big boys.\nAll too often we take for granted how long it takes to make something very personal. Mike Krysztofiak forges his acrylic cube over two years as he manually cuts, sands, drills his masterpiece of LEDs, watercooling and classic style.\nDFI's latest LANParty board is built on the 790FX platform for AMD AM3 CPUs is a yellow and black update to the AM2+ M2RSH. Has DFI changed anything underneath to make it a better buy? Or is it in the same mould with the same limitations? Read on to find out.\nLANParty OC contest \"Project Europa\"\nWe've got photos straight from DFI Taiwan of one of its next generation P55 motherboards.\nDFI's 'dark' 790FX motherboard features the latest SB750 southbridge from AMD and promises the usual crazy DFI overclocking and shenanigans. We drop the new Phenom II X4 940 CPU in to see what it's truly capable of.\nIn a step away from the norm for P45, DFI has made a cute little micro-ATX motherboard that it dubs its \"Junior\". Except, this JR model still supports CrossFire and has a DFI belly - do good P45 motherboards come in small packages? Let's find out."
"Tony Blair gave Kazakhstan\u2019s autocratic president advice on how to manage his image after the slaughter of unarmed civilians protesting against his regime.\nIn a letter to Nursultan Nazarbayev, obtained by The Telegraph, Mr Blair told the Kazakh president that the deaths of 14 protesters \u201ctragic though they were, should not obscure the enormous progress\u201d his country had made.\nMr Blair, who is paid millions of pounds a year to give advice to Mr Nazarbayev, goes on to suggest key passages to insert into a speech the president was giving at the University of Cambridge, to defend the action.\nYou know what\u2019s really sad? The night it became clear that Blair was going to be prime minister I was in Trondheim working with a bunch of Labourites and we all went out dancing to celebrate.\nThe purity trolls here in America think they are so disappointed by Obama the allegedly bloodthirsty third way neoliberal tyrant, but they have no idea how bad it can get."
"Tummy aches be warned, the doctor is in!\nIt\u2019s an unusually cold week in Honeysuckle Hollow and your Li\u2019l Woodzeez animal friend has a fever! Pull on their favorite sweater, help your favorite critter up, and get their favorite can of chicken noodle soup ready. Even though love never hurts, it sounds like your friend might need some extra help. Bundle up your friend and hobble over to the Li\u2019l Woodzeez Walk-in Health ClinicTM.\nWhen you arrive for your appointment, you and your animal pal will see that the Li\u2019l Woodzeez Walk-in Health ClinicTM has everything that you and your little one might need for your little animal toys. There\u2019s nothing scarier than a sick critter after all! Take a seat in one of the miniature plastic seats while your Li\u2019l Woodzeez animal figurine (sold separately) waits to hear from the doctor. Take a moment to learn more about the body by playing with the miniature tooth model or using the scale to measure your miniature critter; there\u2019s plenty of medical equipment sitting around this doctor\u2019s office for you and your friends to explore and discover. If your Li\u2019l Woodzeez pal is really sick or needs more doctor supervision, help them change into one of the Walk-in Health Clinic medical gowns and tuck them into the cozy patient bed. When they wake up tomorrow they\u2019ll find a fresh apple and nice hot bowl of soup waiting for them.\nThis is the perfect place for anyone visiting Honeysuckle Hollow to get a quick check-up for when they aren\u2019t feeling right, or for when they need some tips on how to stay healthy. With so many different tools, you\u2019ll be a Li\u2019l Woodzeez health professional in no time! And who knows; you might even have a clinic of your own when you grow up. In the meantime, why not have some fun in the Li\u2019l Woodzeez Walk-in Health ClinicTM."
"Montgomery Community Media is hosting a seven week Multimedia Producing Class beginning on Tuesday, February 12, 2019 from 6:30 to 9 p.m.\nProducing is the creative organization and implementation of ideas, from concept development to distribution. Producing media for multiple platforms is the way of the future. In this class, participants will create multimedia content on location, in our studios and manage edit sessions for individual production segments that will be shared on multiple distribution platforms.\nIn this class, students will create and produce video segments by pitching story ideas, shooting a segment in the field with a videographer, managing edit sessions and producing a studio segment for an MCM produced show. Participants will learn all aspects of the creative organization it takes to be a Producer!\nNo previous television production experience needed, but this is an active training experience, so participants are expected to work on projects (research, site survey, scriptwriting, etc.) outside of class time to meet production deadlines.\nGood morning Roy - that really sounds like a great bargain. I hope people take advantage of this offering.\nGood morning Roy. If I were closer and not retired, this would have my interest! Enjoy your day!\nAre you taking this class, Roy? Not quite my \"scene.\" I just prefer to call in a professional when I need one.\nGood morning Roy. If I lived a little closer I would definitely attend this class.\nAlways something going on in Montgomery County, and I always like reading about it Roy!\nRoy, this would be a very helpful class, and bet it is well attended.\nSounds like such a great class for those in your area, I know that everyone that attends will learn a lot.\nI will love to know more about your class.Can we join online?\nYou need to click on the link for their website with any questions. It appears that this program is designed for a classroom setting.\nThat multimedia producing class should be very valuable to people in your vicinity, Roy."
