"This is an all embracing legal document setting out the terms and conditions for a club, group or society as an unincorporated association. By that, we mean any association of two or more people, who have come together to form a club to pursue a common social or recreational purpose. Mutual rights and responsibilities arise from the rules which members agree to \u2013 that is, this agreement.\nThis document provides for how the club will be constituted, who controls its structure, administration and funds as well as setting out its purposes, aims and goals. In law, this type of group is called an \u2018unincorporated association\u2019 because, unlike a company, it has not been \u2018incorporated\u2019. Thus, it has no legal identity of its own, beyond the identity of the individual members. These members of course, require rules by which to regulate their association in the pursuit of their common goals. So if you organize a society, club, group or association of any kind, you will need a document such as this.\nWhether you wish to improve the building structure, staffing, services and facilities of any hospital or similar care home, provide a team of volunteer drivers to enable patients who do not need an ambulance to travel between their homes and the hospital free of charge, lend help and support to families of persons in the hospital or promote a healthy lifestyle to those living in a particular area, or have any other similar cause, this document is suitable."
"I was delighted to. Then I drove her 1,000 Klms home to the Outpost.\nMoshi the cat is less thrilled. She has, since Pili\u2019s arrival yesterday evening, worn an expression of outraged \u2018What the F***??!!\u2018. She has spat alot in Pili\u2019s direction, stalked about the house bearing a demeanour that says it all, \u2018Who the hell is that?\u2019 and hurled feline abuse that makes my hair, and hers, stand on end.\nNot Pili\u2019s though, she thinks it\u2019s all part of the fun; that she has discovered the back door is safely mosquito meshed heightens her enjoyment: she can torment Moshi by hurling herself at the mesh and barking without the slightest risk of getting her eyes clawed out.\nShe would love to chase Scal around the garden, Scal who isn\u2019t as outraged as Moshi but is a little nervous of the newcomer so not ready to be chased, she hasn\u2019t bought me back any of the flamboyant pods I throw for her but my, she makes me laugh.\nSomebody said to me this week, \u2018you\u2019re too quiet\u2019.\nAfraid that if I do, start saying, I might revert to default: tediously Minding Gaps.\nBut I have. Let go.\nThat\u2019s the easier, not to say easy, and inevitable bit.\nIt\u2019s the ratting-around-void that\u2019s hard.\nFor so long children have dictated and directed my day that in their absence it is difficult not to flail, not to wonder what to do next.\nSo I find shape to long hours in the tiniest things. I rescue a startling turquoise \u2013 and startled \u2013 kingfisher from the pool which he mistook for a tropical swamp such is its pea-greeness. He was cold and shivered and gasped so that I worried he might die. I fished him out and lay him in the sun to warm and locked that cats up so that he was safe from lurking predators.\nAnd an hour later he was gone. Flown. I rejoiced.\nYesterday I watched him swoop into the same swampy depths. He was more careful this time.\nI found a hedgehog one morning, valiantly swimming in circles, tiny feet paddling to keep him afloat. I fished him out too, and he curled instantly into a tight ball until he thought I wasn\u2019t looking and then he scuttled \u2013 Mrs Tiggywinkle like \u2013 beneath sunbaked stones to slumber.\nAnd then blessedly the rain came down and washed the spiders out of the flamboyant (and into the peagreen pool so that I fished them out as well, but too late for they were stiff and upside down) and rinsed the world clean so that the flamboyant blossom was ruby red again and bled damply onto the lawn, so that the leaves were glossy green.\nRetired and Crazy wants to know what a Sallyworm is. I built my first with an old friend when I was younger than my youngest is now \u2013 and boarding school incarcerated. Sally is maniupulated to give context to time, let you think you can manage it, which is very important when it stretches overwhelmingly and loosely in front of you. Sally\u2019s made of segments, each accounts for a single day. You can cruelly rip her segments off at bedtime or \u2013 more gently \u2013 strike a line through the relevant day\u2019s circle. I have not constructed one for some time; the last I counted days down on was the one Hat drew for me, in my 09 diary, when she went away to England 3 weeks ahead of me.\nI think I might make one now. Give some structure to my day.\nSome definition to my weeks."
"These September 11, 2001 photos were sent to me by Tim Powers, a very old and dear friend. After I reviewed them, I was moved to add them to my web site.\nLet's please not forget the men and woman that were lost in this despicable act of violence, including the 100's of individuals that were NOT in harms way and unselfishly rushed into hell to help . . . many never came out.\nThe outrage we feel should also apply to the continuing escalation of domestic terrorism we have experienced by radical hate-mongers with no tolerance for other views.\nJust as international terrorism is supported and encouraged directly and indirectly by the fringe of religious, social and political groups, so is our home grown version of terrorism. They teach hate and radicalize their children . . . and the cycle continues.\nWe have the good fortune to live in a free society and that freedom does present challenges when dealing with this type of hate bating . . . but we need to keep trying and not give up.\nLet's all work harder to be more vocal in condemning these disturbed perpetrators and those using the airways and the internet to give them direct and as well as more subtle encouragement. We will not like the social consequences of doing nothing and allowing this behavior to continue.\n\"Osama Bin Laden is dead\" President Obama announced Sunday night in a televised address to the nation. The mastermind of the 911 attacks was killed by a small team of Navy SEALs as the result of a U.S. operation launched in Abbottabad, Pakistan against the compound where Bin Laden was hiding. The SEALs took possession of his body and buried him at sea.\nThe word SEAL is an abbreviation for SEa, Air and Land. They are part of the Naval Special Warfare Command (NSWC) and were formerly referred to as SEAL Team 6. They are based in Dam Neck, Virginia (outside of Virginia Beach, Virginia).\nSEALs are considered the most highly trained counter-terrorism force in the world. SEAL Team 6 is comprised of the most elite of the SEALs (so, they are the elite of the elite).\nNOT WANTED ANY MORE . . .\nDeclassified Photos of the horror in lower Manhattan on 11 Sept 2001."
