"Award-winning artist Ty Herndon has released his rendition of the Christmas classic, \u201cO Holy Night.\u201d The track was produced by Herndon, orchestrated by Caleb Collins and features Christian and Gospel vocalist, Crystal Lewis. The track marks Lewis\u2019 first studio recording in over two years. Listen to the song here.\nHerndon and Lewis paired the release of the track with an official music video. View the video here. On Saturday, Dec. 1, Herndon will debut the song at the Nashville Christmas Parade. Hosted by Kid Rock, the parade will be broadcasted live on News 2 (WKRN) from 9 a.m. to 11 a.m. The parade will also air again on Dec. 2 from noon to 2 p.m. Tickets for the parade are available here.\nIn addition to the release of the new holiday single, Herndon has released three dance tracks including a remake of his hit song, \u201cLiving in a Moment,\u201d an original song written by Erick Halbig, \u201cThat Kind Of Night,\u201d an upbeat cover of Marc Cohn\u2019s \u201cWalking in Memphis,\u201d and Whitney Houston\u2019s \u201cI Wanna Dance with Somebody.\u201d The tracks are a collaboration with DJ Lil Steve and were intended to be light and fun tracks for Herndon to perform at the many festivals he plays around the world.\nThese new tracks are only the start of what Herndon has planned for the coming year. In January, the multi-talented vocalist will be releasing a covers album which will include re-imagined and re-cut versions of five of his chart-topping singles, as well as a blues version of \u201cDelta Dawn\u201d by Tanya Tucker. Through the remainder of 2019 Herndon will release two additional projects including a jazz classics duets album in March and a new full-length Country album in December.\nAbout Ty Herndon: Ty Herndon\u2019s career has produced more than four million in album sales, a Grammy nomination, Dove Award and multiple No. 1 singles on the Country charts, including \u201cWhat Mattered Most,\u201d \u201cLiving in a Moment\u201d and \u201cIt Must Be Love.\u201d Among his nine studio albums and 17-charted singles are the Top 10 hits, \u201cI Want My Goodbye Back,\u201d \u201cLoved Too Much,\u201d \u201cA Man Holding On (To a Woman Letting Go)\u201d and \u201cHands of a Working Man.\u201d Most recently, Herndon debuted his most ambitious album to date, titled House on Fire. He made history when he hosted the first-of-its-kind country music event, The Concert For Love and Acceptance. The event, designed to bring attention and support to at-risk youth, has received national attention from Boston Globe, Rolling Stone, Entertainment Tonight, and more. Keep up with the latest on Ty Herndon and his music at www.tyherndon.com or follow him on Facebook, Twitter, and Instagram."
