"I am a co-leader of my local Appleton, Wisconsin chapter of the Rising Tide Society, a group of creative entrepreneurs who come together in the spirit of community over competition. We are all about providing free and low-cost education as a means to lift each other up in business. Each month, we gather on the second Tuesday and talk about a common theme in business. Last month around this time, we discussed the topic of Client Experience.\nEver since then, my awareness has been heightened and I have reflected on my own experiences as a customer in many settings. I can, of course, name a few poor or mediocre experiences, but what good does that do? I want to really show off the things that left a positive impact on me!\nMade my Mee, Appleton, WI: I contacted Michelle, owner of Made by Mee, to see if she could make me a custom crocheted lion hood by Halloween for our toddler to wear as part of her costume. What I loved, beside the ridiculously adorable finished product, was that Michelle had stellar communication skills. She gave me an honest estimate of how long it would take to finish the project based on other items in her production queue. Also, she noted my ideas and color preferences and made exactly what I was looking for! Lastly, she personally delivered the hood to me in a gift bag. Now this, my friends, is how to run a handmade goods business!\nSmith Pharmacy, Little Chute, WI: After getting prescription medication at national pharmacy stores for years and years, I heard through the grapevine of this absolute gem of a store. Smith Pharmacy is a no-frills pharmacy located about 15 minutes away from me. Although I would rather not drive all that way just to pick up medicine, I figured I would check it out at least once. After my visit, I thought, \u201cWhere have you been all my life?!\u201d Seriously, I was amazed. My prescription was approximately $300 per month at a national chain and it was $18 here. The staff were so helpful, setting up a monthly mail delivery service (for no extra charge). So I can get what I need A: for the same price B: delivered to my house and C: on time so I never miss a dose. Lastly, they had a free Ms. PacMan game, small toy area, and free lollipops for the kids to make wait even easier. Thank goodness for local businesses who think about their customers!\nBest Buy, Appleton, WI: This weekend, our microwave finally kicked the bucket and needed to be replaced. I swear this thing has been trying to kill me for years, so I am glad. I dragged my whole family to Best Buy to look at new microwaves, completely expecting the shopping process to take forever, across multiple stores. When we got to the appliance section, an associate connected me to the Appliance Guru, who brought me to his computer and asked me several important questions. He essentially narrowed down my search to the exact model I needed and lo and behold, it was in stock! He automatically did price match searching without my asking, saving me $20, and brought the unit up to the front to wait for us while we finished shopping. This whole process took less than ten minutes (hooray!) and my kiddos barely had time to complain. Checkout was easy and one of the associates helped load it into our vehicle.\nI wanted to share experiences from three very different businesses, of three very different scales. All three left a positive impact on my shopping experience and it was all due to one thing: those people always seemed to be focused on providing quality customer service.\nI am looking forward to sharing more business reviews in the future, diving a little deeper into what I learned from my experiences. I hope you join me on my journey!"
"As a substantial participant in the motion that aided create financial investment crowdfunding via JOBS Act regulation, and also as the CEO of Crowdfunder, I have actually heard there\u2019s some confusion available regarding exactly what crowdfunding means these days, just what the various crowdfunding websites do, and also that they are for.\nTo clean up any confusion, right here\u2019s some straightforward info concerning 2 preferred donation-based crowdfunding sites, and also updates on the state of the new globe of investment crowdfunding.\nKickstarter and also Indiegogo, considered both most popular donation-based crowdfunding websites, were established in 2009 and 2007 respectively. They give people as well as imaginative jobs the opportunity to raise cash using on-line donations or pre-purchasing of items or experiences.\nTo be clear, these 2 crowdfunding systems just support donation-based jobs. They do not enable contributors to come to be an investor or an investor, and also do not qualify contributors as recognized investors to join any kind of financial returns. On both Kickstarter as well as Indiegogo, project creators retain 100% control over their product or services.\nIf you want a wider sight of the entire crowdfunding landscape, see this current Forbes item noting the Top 10 Crowdfunding Sites and just what each does finest.\nIt had not been till lately that the JOBS Act was passed, giving backers the capacity to invest on the internet via investment crowdfunding. And also while the Judgments for the JOBS Act are being implemented progressively, Title II of the JOBS Act has actually simply passed a ballot at the SEC which will certainly enable firms to take part in general solicitation since September 23rd this year, although only certified financiers will certainly have the ability to spend.\nExpect rather of little sound in the financial investment crowdfunding/accredited investing globe as of September 23rd kickoff of Title II and the lift on the very long time restriction on basic solicitation.\nWebsites like CircleUp, Crowdfunder.com, and AngelList are offering possibilities for investment crowdfunding (equity, exchangeable notes) as well as will likely participate in allowing choose firms to usually obtain out on the internet, with financial investment deals connected back to their accredited-investor-only investment atmospheres online.\nSince its launch, Kickstarter has actually become one of the leading players in the crowdfunding arena and also has actually assisted fund over 46,000 successful projects. Kickstarter credits their success on its rigorous qualification plan, job curating, and all-or-nothing financing plan.\nProviding particularly toward innovative, project-based projects, all jobs sent to Kickstarter should fit within among the following categories: Art, Comic books, Dance, Style, Style, Film, Food, Gaming, Music, Photography, Publishing, Technology, or Cinema. Only users from the USA, Canada, or the UK could create jobs, though anyone could donate.\nCampaigns for personal interests, charities, or \u201cfund-my-life\u201d projects are not permitted, and also projects that do not satisfy Kickstarter\u2019s qualifications might be denied.\nSo exactly what campaigns function best on the Kickstarter platform? Any type of project that satisfies the above criteria and results in a particular services or product\u2013 such as jobs that lead to a brand-new publication, cd, or independent film.\nSome organisations have actually successfully utilized Kickstarter to money expansion tasks, develop brand-new applications, and buy new devices. Successful jobs establish an affordable goal, meet that objective within the first 30 to 40 days, and deliver all guaranteed contribution benefits promptly.\nKickstarter Statistics (see their Jacksonville stats).\nAccording to Kickstarter, only 10% of tasks end having gotten no pledges, while \u201c81% of tasks that elevated greater than 20% of their objective were effectively funded.\u201d Jobs might compete 60 days, though Kickstarter recommends setting a target date for Thirty Days or much less.\nIn regards to charges, Kickstarter applies a 5% fee for effectively funded tasks, while unsuccessful tasks sustain no fees yet undergo an all-or-nothing policy- which is is exactly what it sounds like; if a task cannot fulfill its funding objective, none of the contribution commitments made are actually refined. According to Kickstarter, this policy guarantees a level of safety and security for job creators and backers.\nThey basically allow for the crowdfunding of anything\u2013 projects, journeys, charities, and also personal desires. Unlike Kickstarter, Indiegogo does not curate campaigns or place restrictions on task developers.\nGenerally, successful Indiegogo projects remain open for 47 days. According to stats given by a recent record published by The Brink, 80% of Indiegogo jobs cannot increase more than 25% of the complete goal. Nevertheless, the site applies a 4% fee to the funds elevated for effective projects, making it a somewhat less costly alternative to Kickstarter.\nWhile the success price of tasks on Indiegogo might be challenging, many users select Indiegogo for its option of Fixed Financing or Flexible Financing options. Flexible Funding enables developers to keep the funds they have increased, for a 9% charge, even if the task is eventually not successful. Creators are held answerable for providing all guaranteed donation advantages.\nUnsuccessful Fixed Funding projects are not billed any kind of fees, designers are not needed to satisfy any donation advantages, and also all contributions are returned. Indiegogo is coming in 2nd to Kickstarter, its remaining power, international audience, and also inclusive policies have proven a wonderful alternative for job makers looking for even more adaptability.\nRaising Investment Online Via Equity Crowdfunding in Jacksonville FL.\nSince the SEC has lastly passed equity crowdfunding rulings, on the internet financial investment is acquiring enormous energy at sites like CircleUp, Crowdfunder.com and AngelList. The dynamics of financial investment crowdfunding share some similarities with the donation-model, but it\u2019s a various game entirely.\nEquity crowdfunding allows backers to gain eventual economic returns on investments, as well as the financial investment scale for companies as well as startups is normally a lot larger than donation-based crowdfunding projects. The experience of funding something for $25 to $50 on impulse is drastically various from taking into consideration the lasting potential customers of a business, and investing $1,000 to $10,000, or extra.\nHowever, a number of the same components at play in successful donation-based crowdfunding campaigns put on exactly what assists own financial investment crowdfunding too. Those consist of:.\nSocial Proof: Recognizing that backs a campaign could assist guide various other possible investors.\nEnergy: Preliminary financing could beget even more financing.\nRecognition: Having raised cash online efficiently could be an evidence point of its very own.\nConsumer Involvement: Individuals who fund you are likewise your customers.\nAs the overall crowdfunding market is anticipated to expand about at a price of doubling year over year, it is readied to quickly expand with the a lot more instant kicking off of Title II (general solicitation and also accredited investing activity online).\nTitle III of the JOBS Act (non-accredited crowdfunding) is probably to be recommended for commenting this Fall and also put to a ballot by the SEC Commissioners at some time at the end of the year or very early 2014.\nSo remain tuned as the crowdfunding for donation as well as financial investment markets continue to expand quickly."
"Anyways onto the post at hand! In the spirit of my resolution to do more strength training this week (for the sake of my knee but also in the hopes of one day having a smoking hot bod\u2026 bahaha just kidding), I put together a \u201cmarathon friendly\u201d circuit workout to do on Tuesday morning. Marathon training and strength training require a delicate balance. I don\u2019t want to blow out my legs lifting when I need them for a difficult run, but at the same time I want to make sure I\u2019m keeping key running muscles toned and ready for injury prevention. I also don\u2019t want to neglect my upper body and core, which are totally crucial to good running posture and injury prevention (mostly core for the injury prevention part).\nI tend to use my off day and my easy run days for my strength training to allow all my energy / focus to be on running on my SOS days (That\u2019s Hanson Method speak for \u201cSomething of Substance\u201d workouts\u2026 basically your hard workouts).\nI incorporated some basic lower body movements and plyometrics (GREAT for runners), a solid upper body workout, and plenty of focus on the core into this approximately 30 minute strength training workout. I did it \u201cfor time\u201d to get my heart rate up and challenge myself. You can totally just do 12 reps each for 3 rounds and not time it."
