"Phoenix Graphics took flight in 1983 in Winter Haven, Florida. We provide a wide variety of creative services \u2013 preprint assistance, digital printing/production materials, advertising, business cards, book cover designs, logos, brochures, merchandise packaging and website design \u2013 for clients locally, nationally and around the world.\nSimply, our business is to produce any type of artwork \u2013 creatively, professionally, reliably and cost effectively. From initial consultation to finished product, our focus is on making you, the client, look good. Quality is central to all we do at Phoenix Graphics.\nWe\u2019re committed to building or enhancing your business or product image. There isn\u2019t a product requirement we can\u2019t satisfy. When we are finished with your project, the job is ready to go to the printer, fully and clearly marked for a hassle-free press run. That\u2019s more than our intention \u2013 it\u2019s our promise. Phoenix Graphics has been built on unique client confidence. The excellence of our highly skilled design staff is evident in thousands of very satisfied clients. They provide our best testimonials.\nTo learn more about us and the creative work we can provide for you, please see the pages that follow.\nTo receive the superlative service our clients have come to expect, please call us at (863) 294-7083.\nUsing the latest design tools to deliver precise graphics for discerning clients.\nWe deliver advanced graphics that are in step with today\u2019s designs \u2013 and tomorrow\u2019s.\nWe enjoy the unique and the different! We love taking your ideas and bringing them to life.\nWe listen to you to insure our designs surpass your vision.\n\"Thank you again for the banner and the brochures. They were spot on perfect! My boss was extremely pleased with the way they turned out.\nWe really appreciate you jumping through hoops to get this done for us.\"\n\"Thank you for making my story come alive! From this partnership, a wonderful friendship has blossomed.\nMay each day, from sunrise to sunset, bring happiness and amazing surprises your way.\"\n\"We want to say thank you for all of the gorgeous work you've done for our bagel shop, Best Bagels in Town. My dad speaks so highly of you and we can understand why. Your work is so nice, and my dad says that you're as nice of a person, too.\"\n\"I am so proud of you! Seriously, you really hit it out of the park on this one! You completely captured what I couldn't see in my mind, and couldn't articulate, but knew I hoped to see! If that isn't the definition of excellence in what you do, I don't know what is!\"\nI worked with Bonnie and was totally happy with the graphics she created. I will use Phoenix Graphics again and highly recommend them!\nThank you so much for the great work you all did for my business. We love our logo! Phoenix Graphics made us look like a million dollars.\nRaziel here. I hope this e-mail finds you well and creative as usual.\nThis is it. That's what I saw in my vision and it's all thanks to your incredible listening ability, your extraordinary creative input and your impressive technical knowledge.\nI can sincerely say that this is exactly what I had in mind and it is such a privilege to have someone as dedicated and passionate about her work as you and no doubt your team.\nThank you so much is all I can say but words cannot express the awe inspiring and deeply touching gratitude both myself and my sweet darling wife have toward you, and the beautiful (and urgently needed in this day & age) company that you've worked so hard to build to what it is. Now my soul mate wishes to say a few words, be at peace with the world my dear and I am excited to work with you again for the website! Thank you!\nHi Bonnie, Soraya here. My dear husband does have a way with words, I don't know how to thank you for all that you've done. We've had this dream of creating a product that would help our fellow humans in whatever way we can and it is because of you that we can now move forward with our dreams. Thank you once more from the bottom of our hearts.\nI wanted to reach out and let you both know that you did a great job with our label. It looks exactly how I imagine it could. I am also impressed with the speed in which this project was completed. Great work all around. I will be in touch shortly for our next label."
