"When I was younger, I loved going to the Strasenburgh Planetariumin Rochester, NY. It was a portal that helped my worries float away into the Milky Way.\nWhether losing myself at the planetarium, staring at my bedroom ceiling\u2019s solar system, or being blown away by the night sky of Australia\u2019s Outback, my problems always seemed smaller against the context of the universe.\nSri Sri Ravi Shankar reminded me of this during the World Happiness Summit.\nIt\u2019s natural to see our problems as bigger than life. Their significance and our unhappiness grow as they fester in our heads. But in reality, they are much smaller than our inner critic leads us to believe.\n\u201cIf you follow joy, misery follows you. If you follow wisdom, joy follows you.\u201d- Sri Sir Ravi Shankar.\nYou just may see the wisdom and perspective that you are seeking.\nBe Happy and Have Fun Storming the Castle!\nP.S. If you wish to learn more World Happiness Summit wisdom, circle back or join our mastermind guest day at 11 am today by clicking Happy."
