"Within the global UCB IT organization, the IT Finance and Procurement group is looking for a unique individual to strengthen our team in the Analytics and Reporting domain.\nOur Finance and Procurement function has been on the forefront in implementing innovative digital solutions leveraging Advanced Analytics and Artificial Intelligence algorithms. For taking this innovation to the next level, we are looking for an Analytics lead to deliver impact.\nAs a trusted Business Partner, you will connect regularly with your stakeholders to identify improvements and innovation in the financial analytics area and contribute in building a common project roadmap that positively impacts our patients.\nGiven all analytics and reporting initiatives start from the data, as the Analytics lead, you will master the Finance Data Foundation and Flows. By working with the system Solution Experts and Data owners, you will help to create the visibility on the Finance Datasets and contribute in deepening UCB\u2019s ability to unlock the power of data.\nNext to creating and owning this Data Foundation, you will act as a Connector and Translator in core analytics initiatives. You are enthusiastic to shape and drive IT Finance analytics initiatives. You speak the language of both technical team as well as the business partners and as such connect the different domains. You like a challenge and take accountability to deliver.\nPartner with your stakeholders: connect and communicate with your stakeholders to understand and identify new business requirements and possibilities for innovation. Together you build a data analytics strategy and common roadmap.\nDeliver Projects & Support: Act as the Connector / Translator on key analytics projects and closely collaborate with all parties involved (Finance and IT, internal and external partners), following the UCB IT project methodology. You take ownership to deliver on time, budget and with the required quality.\nDrive Innovation: Follow market trends and industry best practices with the aim of sharing the acquired knowledge inside UCB and of applying it to propose innovative solutions.\nAct as a IT ambassador: Actively take part in the implementation of the IT analytics strategy. Ensure compliance of the solutions to global process and legal requirements, follow validation guidelines and standard operating procedures.\n4+ years of experience with Data Warehouse and Analytics / Reporting solutions. The core solutions you will be exposed to are mainly SAP BW (Hana), Qlik, R, Cognos BI and IBM TM1. Knowledge of SAP ERP (FI/CO) is considered a plus.\nYou understand key financial concepts and have worked in this area already. Terms as Forecasting, Opex, P&L, COGS, balance sheets,\u2026 don\u2019t scare you."
"We\u2019ve been busy adding features to Tddium in the last few days, including MySQL 5.1, Sqlite3, and Spork. Redis and MongoDB are implemented and about to be released. More importantly, we\u2019re now using Tddium internally on a regular basis and I have to say it is a big step forward. Why? Well it certainly is nice to have a fast, hosted test environment, but the big reason for me right now is isolation. Each test script runs in its own thread with its own isolated environment: it gets its own Postgres, MySQL, or Sqlite database; it gets its own Spork DRb for rspec or cucumber; it gets its own fresh set of loaded modules. In short, each test script runs in its own complete environment."
