"Realize Colorado, a destination management company, recently announced that Tina Schwab has joined its staff as director of sales. In her new position, Schwab will be responsible for business development, working with local hotel owners and developing client relationships.\nSchwab hasn\u2019t always worked in the tourism and hospitality industry; after more than 25 years as a sales and marketing professional in several business sectors, Schwab decided to change career paths in 2013 when she took on a sales manager position with Visit Vail Valley.\nSchwab has since served two terms as director of strategic alliances for the Colorado Society of Association Executives and Meeting Professionals International Rocky Mountain Chapter. Additionally, she was inducted into Colorado Meetings + Events magazine\u2019s Hall of Fame as an up-and-coming supplier in 2017.\n\u201cBeing a Colorado native, I am passionate about the economic vitality of our state and fully understand the importance of tourism and group travel. I have met and worked alongside some of the best in our industry, and it is a pleasure to join the talented Realize Colorado team,\u201d Schwab says. \u201cI look forward to continue promoting Colorado as the premier destination for meetings and events.\u201d Schwab is based in Realize Colorado\u2019s Denver office. The Global DMC Partner provides corporate, incentive, nonprofit and association groups with a long list of destination services throughout the Centennial State.\nCherry Creek hotel, Halcyon, has announced Jason Delcamp its new general manager. Delcamp will be responsible for all operations, performance and strategic direction of the 154-room hotel as it begins a new chapter with hotel operator Makeready."
