"06.35 am \u2013 Woke up, had breakfast from 7-Eleven, took a dump, showered and packed up.\nMy favourite bottled soy bean milk.\nChecked out the check in information to make sure that our flight is departing as scheduled.\nWhile queuing, I just couldn\u2019t help but notice that we were the only Chinese looking Malaysians.\nAbout 5 minutes later, we got our boarding passes.\n09.00 am \u2013 As we already had our breakfast back at the hotel, we went directly towards our departure gate to wait for boarding.\n09.28 am \u2013 Walked to our plane. Excited as ever!\nStill, I cannot understand AirAsiaX\u2019s decision to eventually cancel it\u2019s KUL-DEL route in April 2012. The flight was almost full! Yes, the airport tax increase means extra burden for passengers but the thing is it applies to all other airlines as well. AirAsia will still be much cheaper compared to full service airlines.\nEnjoyed the first flight hour reading Travel 3Sixty.\nFilled in the India Arrival Card for foreigners.\nSleeping like a baby in its mother\u2019s womb.\nHad Airasia\u2019s chicken butter rice for brunch. Delicious!\nNot long after, Vivian had her chicken briyani. Delicious!\nTurned the clock back 2\u00bd hours as India was +5\u00bd GMT while Malaysia was +8 GMT.\n*All times after this is in IST.\nWe knew we were in Delhi when we saw the fog that Delhi\u2019s winter is famous for.\n01.12 pm \u2013 Arrived at New Delhi, India and was surprised to find Indira Gandhi International Airport to be so clean and modern.\nThe giant symbolic hand gestures at immigration called mudras, commonly found in Buddhism, Hinduism and yoga greeting arriving passengers. And though almost all counters were open, the crowd lining up was HUGE. My guess is several planes arrived at almost the same time.\n01.32 pm \u2013 Collected our luggage from the belt.\nThe terminal was so modern and clean. What a sparkling first impression it gave us!\n01.44 pm \u2013 Made our way towards the Airport Metro Express.\nBought ourselves a one way ticket from the airport to New Delhi Railway Station for INR 80 which I think is pretty cheap compared to Malaysia\u2019s KLIA Express for MYR 35.\nEverything to this point still looked bright, clean and modern.\n02.09 pm \u2013 Inside the coach that looks pretty much like KLIA Express\u2019s.\nThe scenery along the 20 minute journey consisted mostly of roads.\n02.34 pm \u2013 Exiting the New Delhi Railway Airport Express station.\nAt the entrance of New Delhi Railway Station.\nAh, this was the point where our bubble burst. India smelled like what India was supposed to smell like. Porters coming up to you asking to carry your bags for a fee. Pair of eyes everywhere staring at you. Hordes of people everywhere.\n02.59 pm \u2013 Left New Delhi Railway in search of Paharganj where our temporary hotel was supposed to be at. Lost our way for about 10 minutes while being constantly followed by tuk tuk drivers persuading us to take a ride with them.\nIt wasn\u2019t long before we found the backpacker haven of Paharganj.\n03.26 pm \u2013 There were so many tiny, narrow lanes all over Paharganj that it was so difficult for us to find New King DX Hotel. When I arrived, the entrance to the hotel gave Vivian and I such an uneasy feeling. I booked a room at New King because it had one of the cheapest double rooms in Delhi and I only needed to use it for a nap and a shower.\nWhen we arrived we were told that there were renovations going on in the dorm room so our double bed was given to others. We were upgraded to another hotel within the vicinity under the same ownership.\n03.48 pm \u2013 New Hindustan DX.\nThe business card to get us back to the hotel in case we needed to use a taxi.\n04.38 pm \u2013 Found Malhotra Restaurant from the excellent online Indian restaurant directory called Zomato.\nOrdered vegetables, chicken, eggs and naan.\nOur first meal tasted real good.\nGot myself a Vodafone prepaid sim. I was actually curious as to what food/drink people were queuing for outside of Bhalla Cafe but didn\u2019t pursue it any further as I wanted to stick to the golden rule for avoiding diarrhea in India. No street food no matter what.\n06.03 pm \u2013 Arrived back to our hotel for a few hours worth of rest.\n08.16 pm \u2013 After a warm shower, we packed up and got ready to leave for Jodhpur.\n08.32 pm \u2013 Found ourselves a tuktuk to bring us to the train station.\n09.06 pm \u2013 Sarai Rohilla Railway Station, one of 6 railway stations in Delhi, where our train was scheduled to depart.\nFound ourselves in an eating place located along the narrow lanes opposite the train station.\nAs we did months of homework before coming to India, ordering in a non-English speaking environment was much easier.\nJeera rice, an Indian dish consisting of rice and cumin seeds.\nThe vegetarian rice was actually tastier and more nutritious.\n09.55 pm \u2013 Locating our coach and berth took quite an effort. We could see other confused foreigners trying to find theirs as well. Lol.\nFinally, about 10 minutes later, we were aboard our coach.\nVivian took the upper bunk while I took the lower bunk. I slept for a whole 8 hours out of the 10 hours we were on the tracks. I think the continuous motion of the train coupled with the white noise of the wheels made sleeping a little more comfortable although every time I took an overnight train, there were loud snorers around.\nHonestly, I found the toilets in class AC2 of Rajasthan S Krant, our train name, to be really clean! It looked cramp but smelled alright."
"We Rock the Spectrum Redondo Beach is committed to providing a safe, nurturing, and fun environment to foster learning, exploration and safe sensory experiences. Through our nonprofit My Brother Rocks The Spectrum Foundation, we provide social skills groups and activities for children across the spectrum.\nWe Rock the Spectrum Redondo Beach provides children with a fun and motivational environment to help them in the areas of strength, movement, sensory processing, communication, positive behavior modification, social interactions, and self-care skills. Our unique equipment assists all children in their neurological growth and development.\nWe LOVE this place and we rock the spectrum has become our second home and our go to when we want our four year old daughter who is autistic to play and get some energy out. It's so nice to come here and feel welcome and not feel weird about who will be judging my kid because she does some things a little differently. We come here a lot just to play or for play dates. The space is amazing, just like an occupational therapy room with lots of swings, a huggle pod, big trampoline with safety net, rock climbing wall and a zip line. All types of toys and swings for kids with sensory needs or just to play in a safe environment. My daughter loves it here and it's a nice place to come when you don't feel like dealing with the regular playground and the parents and kids who don't understand children with special needs. They also have an awesome music room that my daughter LOVES! Tons of cool drums, bongos, tambourines, steel drums and microphones. They do drum circles a couple times a day and my daughter loves it. The other day she hopped on the mic and started singing her heart out. She can truly just chill and be herself here and I just love this place so much. Also Sharelle and Sabina the owners are super nice and always so welcoming and accommodating to us and all the children. We LOVE we rock the spectrum! All kids are welcome too. It's an amazing place and I'm so thankful this place is open.\nMy 2 Special Needs Son's Jayden & Donnie love this place! Unlike any other indoor kids gym. The Set up is very much like an Occupational Therapy Playground Sharelle & Sabina are very kindhearted, fun loving ladies that not only Manage & own the place but actually interact with the kids. I haven't seen this kind of interaction at the other We Rock the Spectrum Kids Gyms. Nor do they have a Free To Be Me Music Studio Room. Quite the Bonus!Not too many places I feel safe to bring my 2 boys alone. Except here. This is our new 2nd home. We love you guys! Thank you so much for the Beautiful Drum!we definitely will always come here and recommend others to this place.\nWe Rock Redondo is the PERFECT place for a party! We hosted my son's 6th birthday party at We Rock, and it was so much fun! Sharalle and Sabina were easy to work with as we planned for the big day, and they both helped in countless ways throughout the party. We Rock was the perfect environment for our all of our guests, including parents. One mom told me that our drum circle proved therapeutic as she pounded out her frustrations on her drum and felt great at the end of the party. How often can parents say that a kid's birthday party is refreshing?? We had 20 kids at the party so the gym felt busy, but not crowded. We Rock's party options are very reasonably priced, providing an excellent alternative to other party venues in the area. We can't wait to go back!\nI've been to several We Rock's gyms yet haven't met staff who's as enthusiastic and passionate as the owners Sabina and Sharalle! They constantly engage with the children with their positivity and energy. And what makes their gym unique is the drum circle led by Sabina, the founder of \"Free To Be Me\" drumming program. Definitely a magical place for children with all abilities!\nThis place is incredible! They have everything here; therapy swings, puzzles, play grocery shopping/store front, drum circles, a giant trampoline, just to name a few! There is a very free, comfortable environment where children of different ages and special needs can safely play and be entertained for hours! I am so happy that I know about this place and look forward to many play dates and ABA sessions here!\nMy daughter enjoys this play gym! It is super clean and there are so many things to do in the space like trampolines, ziplines, drums and train sets. She is a regular here and we are happy to have found this place!\nWhat a gem. A beautifully clean gym space, music room, and art area with ample parking and easy accessibility. My girls are 7, 4.5, and 1.5 and beg to go every day. The owners are magic - kind and loving and truly proud of the important work they are doing. The gym functions like an OT gym for my child who receives OT, and like a fun play zone for the other kids. Amazing amazing amazing. Buy the monthly pass if you can, you won't regret it.\nWe stumbled upon this place while visiting Redondo Beach and were blown away! Great space with fabulous toys and equipment but by far what won us over was the *out of this world* staff! Sabina and Sharelle are very special and kind souls and made our children's' day. We have a 6 year old, almost 4 year old, and 1 year old and everyone enjoyed. Zip line, monkey, bars, trampoline, arts and crafts, balls, trains, all different kinds of swings etc. The music room is special and unique for kids to have a chance to belt out their favorite songs and drum along to the beat. All our children enjoyed. Thank you Sabina! Thank you Sharelle!\nMommy Support Group! RSVP Tell A Friend!\nAmazing Life Changing Co-Ownership Franchise Opportunity!"
