"Georgetown North Dental Group has served Fort Wayne, Indiana and the surrounding community for over 35 years. Our staff includes two doctors and four hygienists. We base our success on friendly service, an open atmosphere, and lasting relationships.\nOur dental office is focused on providing a professional, yet comfortable environment for patients young and old. We use the latest in advanced technologies like 3D imaging to achieve a level of visibility other practices don't have. We show you your results on a large screen to give you access to a new perspective on your dental health.\nOur office is bright and spacious, featuring artwork from local Fort Wayne artist Terry Ratliff. Because of our size and modern surgical suites, we often host seminars and study sessions for implant dentistry involving dentists from Indiana and Ohio.\nDr. Bruick graduated from Snider High School in 1973 and earned a B.A degree at Indiana University in 1977. While at IU, he was granted Phi Beta Kappa membership for academic achievement.\nDr. Dinh is excited to be part of the Georgetown North Dental Group team. He grew up in Fort Wayne, IN and graduated from Bishop Dwenger High School.\nKelly graduated from Indiana University South Bend with an Associate of Science degree in Dental Hygiene and started working at Georgetown North Dental Group in August 1992. She also graduated from IPFW in 1996 with Bachelor's degree in general studies.\nAmi graduated with an Associate of Science Dental Hygiene at IPFW and started at Georgetown North Dental Group in July 1998. She is licensed in local anesthesia.\nAmber earned an Associate of Science degree in dental hygiene from Indiana University-Purdue University Fort Wayne in 2006. She started working at Georgetown North Dental Group in August 2006. She is licensed in local anesthesia.\nKrista graduated with an Associate of Science degree in Dental Hygiene from Indiana University-Purdue University Fort Wayne in 2013. She started working at Georgetown North Dental Care in April 2018. She is licensed in local anesthesia."
