"Our stampede string isn't only for ranchers working cattle on the open range. Anyone who wants to keep their hat from blowing away will find it useful. Like our chin strap, a sliding knot joins together two, four plait braids of kangaroo leather. It is ideal for both our Heritage Collection and Panama hats that do not have chin strap hooks. Two cotter pins slide between the sweatband and the hat body. Once bent, they provide a secure attachment of the stampede string. Our own production, made in the USA.\nDo you live outside the US? Due to strict US export regulations, we are only able to ship kangaroo leather products outside the US by adhering to the US Fish and Wildlife Service export inspection procedures.\nStampede String or Chin Strap?\nIf you purchased an Akubra without Chin Strap Hooks or one of our other fine styles of hats, we recommend our Stampede String.\nIf you have an Akubra not purchased from us, you will have to check to see if it has chin strap hooks inside the crown. The chin strap hooks are put on the Akubra hats especially for us, and many Akubra's available elsewhere do not have the hooks. Our Stampede String is a good alternative for most hats without chin strap hooks.\nPlease watch this short video from our David Morgan on YouTube channel for instructions on how to attach a stampede string to your hat.\nOur Stampede String has two cotter pins which slide between the sweatband and the hat body for easy attachment to a hat.\nHold the cotter pins tightly together and push them through the stitching where the sweatband meets the body.\nPull the pins completely through the base of the sweatband until the braid is firmly against the sweatband.\nSpread the pins outward, as close to horizontal as possible.\nCheck by tugging on the braid."
