be brought to the weigh in via the tournament registered vessel only.\n13. Weigh in location is the Public Ramp on 15th Street in Fort Lauderdale.\n14. All releases must be called in via VHF 72 for statistical purpose.\n15. In the event of a tie the earliest time of the 2nd fish to be weighed will be the tie breaker.\n16. Safety is the each person\u2019s responsibility and all participants fish this tournament at their own risk. In the event of Small Craft Advisory or other unsafe weather conditions the tournament will be rescheduled for the following weekend. Entry fees will not be refunded. The tournament director nor anyone associated with the tournament will be held liable for any loss or injury of anyone. The captain of the vessel assumes liability of all persons or goods.\n17. This is a friendly tournament that is being put on for everyone\u2019s enjoyment. It is not designed to have any type of controversy. NO INTEGRITY ISSUES WILL BE TOLERATED. Immediate disqualification will take place on any boat that even approaches a rule violation.\n18. The weigh master will have final say in any situation.\n20. Polygraph will be available and if it is used the payment will come out of all winnings paid out.\n21. No t-shirts trophies or other prizes that take away from the tournament winnings.\n22. Signing below acknowledges all above."
