"SAN FRANCISCO (AP) \u2014 Pinterest, the digital scrapbooking site, has filed for an initial public offering of stock. That's kicking off the year's IPO season, which is also expected to include Uber, Lyft and messaging app Slack.\nPinterest said in a regulatory filing Friday that it intends to list its stock on the New York Stock Exchange. The company isn't saying how many shares it's selling in the IPO or how much money it intends to raise.\nThe San Francisco-based company had revenue of $756 million and a loss of $63 million last year.\nPinterest has long shunned being labeled a social network. Because of that, it doesn't push users to add friends or build connections. But it's also been able to avoid problems of its larger rivals like Facebook."
"Martin Scorsese's adventure film \u201cHugo\u201d which explores the early days of cinema from a child\u2019s point of view led the 2012 Academy Awards with 11 nominations, including Best Picture and Best Director while \u201cThe Artist\u201d earned 10 as George Clooney and Meryl Streep emerged as frontrunners for best actor and actress. The nominees for Academy Awards 2012 were announced on Tuesday morning, January 24 at the Samuel Goldwyn Theater by Tom Sherak, AMPAS president, and Oscar-nominated actress Jennifer Lawrence. The 2012 Oscars will air on February 26, 2012 at the Kodak Theatre in Hollywood, California and Billy Crystal will serve as host for the evening, replacing Eddie Murphy, who was originally slated to host.\nThe other nominations for Best Picture are The Descendants, The Help, Midnight in Paris, Moneyball, The Tree of Life, War Horse and Extremely Loud and Incredibly Close."
