"Entrance Canopies | Kreider's Canvas Service, Inc.\nCovering over a commercial entranceway and walkway will protect customers from rain snow and ice. Save on salt and shovel less snow. Add removable clear side panels to provide protection from wind, blowing rain and snow in winter. Add a corporate logo or custom graphics. Lighting can be added underneath the awning providing a bright, cheery and safe entrance for clients.\nWalkway canopy fabricated and installed over an entrance for a business in Harrisburg PA. Clients were having trouble identifying which door to use to enter the building. The awning solved this issue while also providing protection from the elements. The dimensions are 40\u2032 long x 10\u2032 wide x 5\u2032 high. Powder coated galvanized steel awning frame attached to structural steel beams. 6 uprights concreted into ground.\nLarge arched shape entrance canopy protects this entrance for clients entering building. Aluminum frame construction with white uprights.\nAn arched entranceway canopy with a large flat front area for lettering. Powder coated aluminum frame resting on heavy duty steel I-beams.\nDecember 2014 Kreider\u2019s installed a large carport awning at Brethren Village Lancaster PA. The framing is all 1\u00d71 and 1\u00d72 galvanized steel tubing fabricated primarily at our shop with the final part being assembled and welded onsite. Separate box panels where added around the perimeter underneath to hide the lacing system. Then a mesh undercover was installed to cover over the framing.\nI am very impressed and love the way your company does business from start to finish."
