"More social website jostling, as AOL upgrades and launches a beta version of AOL Pictures as a direct competitor to Flickr.\nFlickr, if you\u2019ve been hiding in a cave for the past few years, is the photo-sharing website that pretty much caused the phenomenon of content sharing, and was recently taken over by Yahoo.\nWill it work? In the world of social Internet sites, it doesn\u2019t have nearly a silly enough name to be a runaway success. AOL Pictures \u2013 yeah, well, it does what it says, and you know who owns it, but it\u2019s not a daft name is it?\nFor any other cave dwellers out there \u2013 etribes is representing the UK in the personal publishing and photo-sharing arena. We\u2019ve got mobile posting and a nifty deskbar that lets you post pictures to secure galleries without opening a browser. We are also doing our level best in the silly names stakes!"
"Oxford Wedding Photographer Supports Local Netball.\nRecently, I was very pleased when my wedding photography business was asked to support the flourishing sport of netball. Oxfordshire Netball has its centre very close to where I am based in Oxford. It is also home to Oxford City Football Club, who established the site, and now both Junior and Seniors Leagues play netball weekly under floodlights at this superb venue.\nI have stood on the touchline watching my sister play netball on many a freezing cold evening and even been the official scorer! So when The Oxfordshire Netball Development Board sought funding for a touchline shelter for players and coaches, I really felt this was an excellent proposition.\nMy sponsorship arrangement offers great publicity for my wedding photography and I now have my business name proudly emblazoned on a smart new shelter. Pictured above,dry and warm, are some of the development board members trying out the new facility.\nThe ONDB promote the development of netball across our local area. Oxfordshire Netball is affiliated to England Netball, as are over 1,500 Oxfordshire members. The Board brings together volunteers from all aspects of netball in the county. Volunteers are tasked with developing netball in our area and are involved in umpiring, coaching, facility development, school links, talent development, disability and welfare.\nOxfordshire National Development Board works alongside Netball South, England Netball, Oxfordshire Sports Partnership, local authorities, schools and other sporting bodies. This allow players and officials to develop their skills to enhance netball within our county. The end goal is to broaden participation in netball in all locations, for all who want to play."
