"Journal: What are you doing to nurture your life with God these days? How do these verses encourage or speak to that? What is your plan for your spiritual growth going forward?\nReflection: You do not have to do these things; not at all. God does not, I regret to report, give a hoot. You do not have to do these things - unless you want to know God. They work on you, not on him.\nManuel and Annabella Valverde are involved in church planting and leadership training in Guatemala. Manuel started the Francisco Lacueva Theological Seminary (STFL) in 2012 and they now have 14 students. Pray today for an upcoming event in February where Manuel will be leading the ACTS seminar in Cuba."
"I have to confess that I really really love weddings where the groom is totally into it. Totally into the experience, and obviously, totally into marrying the love of his life. It makes such a difference when the groom is expressive in his enthusiasm for the wedding day. And here we have Steve \u2026 and Juana. I will let the photographs speak for themselves, and you can easily see the energy and mischievousness and all the other joyful expressions of this couple, clearly in love.\nJuana and Steve\u2019s wedding day was held at the Rockleigh Country Club \u2013 a venue I like photographing at because of the large gardens and pretty surroundings. The preparation, wedding ceremony and reception all took place at the venue. That left us with enough time for lovely photographs. And here they are. I\u2019m quite proud of this set.\nJuana and Steve, it was a fantastic experience working with you as your wedding photographer. Best wishes for your future together.\nI enjoyed looking through your portfolio here & had a question as to your kit; I wondered what flash combination you use indoors? I use a Nikon SB800 but always find it really difficult to use indoors for the larger room shots without ramping up the ISO which effectively makes the flash act as a fill-in, otherwise the exposure always falls off dramatically further from the lens. Your images seem much more evenly lit indoors therefore I thought that I would ask how you go about it?\nThese two articles should help explain what I do."
