"1. Attach the ends of the leather to one of the flat closures and clamp it down with your pliers until it is secure. I spaced my leather out so that it filled the entire clasp, instead of letting their be space on either side of the leather inside the clasp.\n2. Tape the clasp end to a table or flat surface and braid the leather. Make sure that the front of the leather stays up as you braid.\n3. Once you get to your desired length, (measure your wrist) mine was 7\u2033, then cut the leather and put the other flat clasp on.\n4. Using jump rings attach the magnetic closures to the flat clasp ends. You\u2019re done! wow, that was fast, right?!"
