"6/27/12 I have just purchased StitchMastery software and used it to revise the entire pattern to include easier to read charts and \u2026 drum roll please\u2026written instructions!\n5/10/12. In the border chart move the nupps on the left side up one row from 35/36 to 36/37 to match the right side.\nThe missing stitch symbol is SSSK.\nThanks to all of you who have sent compliments, suggestions and found errors. There have been several changes to the last chart and a note added to the second chart. Please download the new version.\nI have just updated the pattern. There was an error on row 15 of the Dayflower chart. Stitch 5 should be a K2tog, rather than a K.\n2/23/11 I have just updated the pattern. There were corrections to the Chevron chart yesterday. Today there were corrections to row numbers and number or times to repeat the Willow leaves chart. Hopefully no one has knit that far yet. There have also been corrections to the Willow Leaves/Aeolian Flowers Chart.\nLife lines are a good idea. Frogging lace is not much fun.\nThank you all for your enthusiastic support and patient feed back.\nI find that I have to begin charging for this pattern.\nI spend too much time answering messages from people who find it more convenient to message me than to read the pattern."
