"Valli Ehrlich is a Paediatric Speech Pathologist with a Bachelor of Applied Sciences (Speech Pathology) and is a member of Speech Pathology Australia. Valli has extensive experience in the assessment and management of children with communication impairments. She has particular interest in early language, literacy development and phonological awareness. Valli has worked in preschools, early childhood centres, schools and private practice for over 10 years.\nValli has a thorough understanding of the Australian School Curriculum, Early Years Learning Framework (EYLF) as well as the language and literacy skills that pre-school and school-aged clients need to function effectively in the classroom and become confident, competent communicators.\nValli is committed to ongoing professional development and current evidence-based practices to ensure a relevant and targeted approach to best assist children and their families. She has undergone extensive training in procedures and practices, completed a variety of workshops and conferences. Valli is also involved in educator and teacher training, the implementation of language and literacy programs and workshops throughout Australia. One of the most recent projects involved the introduction of language and literacy programs within remote Aboriginal Communities in Warmun, Western Australia.\nValli aims to provide the best functional outcomes for her clients, achieved with structured therapy developing children\u2019s skills through fun, play-based activities, as well as developing parents\u2019 and carers\u2019 skills for continued progress at home. Valli holds a strong belief in holistic management; working collaboratively with paediatricians, allied health professionals and families in the assessment, diagnosis and treatment of children."
"The doctors who deal with everything that has to do with the eye which may include the caring and maintenance of it for it to have a healthy life are called ophthalmologists. Their purpose in your life is to ensure that your eye has the best kind of functionality it should have whether you are young or old. In terms of eyesight, they will help you live as normal as you ought to by performing simple or complex surgeries if that is what is required to keep a good eyesight and they will also prescribe eye glasses or contact lenses. In order to ensure excellent eyesight and longevity, you will usually find a lot of options being offered to you. If you have been struggling with your eyesight because of health problems, an eye doctor will be able to prescribe to you the best way for you to take in order to experience health in that area.\nYour overall physical health is also very dependent on the health of your eyesight. The expertise of a medical eye doctor is very needed when it comes to making sure that your overall health of your eyes is okay. Some of the many options that a medical eye doctor will give you are surgeries, the insertion of contact lenses in your eyes and also eye glasses. The purpose of these options may be to correct an error in your eye, treat a disease in your eye or rectify a problem which will lead to you having a better experience with your vision.\nOne way you can be able to find an ophthalmologist in your area is by use of an online directory.\nApproaching a neighbor, friend or a family member who may have had to visit an ophthalmologist before for one reason or the other is another thing that you should do. When you approach your loved one with this kind of need, they will be able to refer you to a good ophthalmologist especially if they have ever had to utilize the services of one. If they have never had to visit this kind of a doctor, then they may have people close to them who may have to utilize these doctors\u2019 services. Before you move on to the next notion, make sure that you have gone through all your loved ones and that none of them seems to have a clue about this.\nThis next available option is an option whereby you would have to look for a recommendation from any doctor that you may know."
"The West Nordic Council is a parliamentary co-operation between Iceland, Greenland and the Faroe Islands. 18 Members of Parliament form the Council, six from each member country. The Council convenes twice a year, for its Annual General Meeting and its Theme Conference. The Council\u00b4s Standing Committee organizes and conducts the Council\u2019s general work and activities throughout the year, with the support of the Council\u00b4s Secretary-General and the Secretaries of the three national delegations. The West Nordic Council\u00b4s Secretariat is located in Reykjav\u00edk, Iceland, within the International Secretariat of the Parliament of Iceland.\nThe West Nordic Council was founded in 1985 in recognition of the many common interests the three countries share in the region. The Council is one of the oldest on-going pan-arctic cooperation mechanisms in the world. Focus areas have included sustainable development, environmental affairs, natural resources, transport, infrastructure, search and rescue, climate change, free trade, security and defense, public health, culture, education, youth and Arctic affairs.\n\u2013 Promote the common interests of the West Nordics.\n\u2013 Strengthen cooperation between the West Nordic governments.\n\u2013 Promote West Nordic interests within Nordic cooperation.\n\u2013 Strengthen cooperation with and between other West Nordic organizations.\n\u2013 Strengthen cooperation with other parliamentary organizations, including the Conference of Parliamentarians of the Arctic Region and the European Parliament.\n\u2013 Adopting resolutions submitted directly to the three national parliaments for approval and subsequently implemented by the appropriate ministers in the governments of the three countries.\n\u2013 Cooperating with the West Nordic governments.\n\u2013 Actively participating and contributing to Nordic co-operation within the Nordic Council.\n\u2013 Facilitating interaction between and sharing information with other West Nordic organizations, including the West Nordic Foundation and the North Atlantic Co-operation Committee, NORA.\n\u2013 Observing and contributing to the work of the Conference of Parliamentarians of the Arctic Region and its Standing Committee.\n\u2013 Exchanging views with the SINEEA delegation of the European Parliament (EP) at annual meetings between the West Nordic Council and the EP.\n\u2013 Organizing conferences and meetings.\n\u2013 Sharing information on West Nordic issues, locally, regionally and internationally, with amongst others the general public, regional and international partners and the West Nordic governments.\nCollectively the nations of the North Atlantic make up a very large geographical area including enormous sea territories. The vast blue sea is to the West Nordic Countries what green fields and woodlands are to other countries. The Faroe Islands and Iceland were populated by Norse Vikings from around the 9th century whereas the history of Greenland populated with Inuits dates back more than 5000 years. The Norse settlers arrived in Greenland around 982 where they lived for almost 500 years. The special cultural and geographic conditions of the Faroe Islands, Greenland and Iceland were subject to political discussions in the early 1980s. Subsequently, the West Nordic countries established a joint parliamentary organisation. The chief aim is to cooperate on common challenges and interests in the West Nordic region and the North Atlantic, in collaboration with other countries and organisations.\nThe West Nordic Council\u2019s work and activities is organised and led by the Presidium, consisting of three representatives from the member delegations.\nThe Faroe Islands delegation of the West Nordic Council is appointed by the Faroese Parliament.\nThe Greenland delegation of the West Nordic Council is appointed by Inatsisartut \u2013 the Parliament of Greenland.\nThe Iceland delegation of the West Nordic Council is appointed by the Parliament of Iceland.\nIt is not possible for the West Nordic Council to grant direct financial aid or support to projects."
